+<section class="seo-about" aria-labelledby="seo-about-h"><h2 id="seo-about-h">Ledger — free cash flow, GST and BAS tracker for tradies</h2><p>Who owes you, where the money&#x27;s going and what the BAS will look like — GST on a cash basis. Free money console for Australian tradies, from BlueprintAU.</p><h3>Does Ledger replace my accountant or Xero/MYOB?</h3><p>No. Ledger is a cash-flow and GST view for the owner, not a general ledger. It gives you the day-to-day numbers and a BAS estimate; your accountant still lodges. Export to Excel at quarter end and hand it over.</p><h3>Is the BAS estimate on a cash or accruals basis?</h3><p>Cash basis — GST is counted when money is actually received or paid, which is how most small trade businesses under the turnover threshold report. The figure is an estimate to plan around, not a lodgement.</p><h3>Is Ledger free?</h3><p>Yes, free forever. No subscription, no user limits, no card. Your data stays in your browser on your own device.</p><h3>Does it connect to my bank?</h3><p>No. Ledger deliberately has no bank feed — you enter or import expenses, and invoices flow in from Foreman. That&#x27;s what keeps it free and keeps your bank credentials out of a third-party app.</p><h3>Can I import my existing invoices and expenses?</h3><p>Yes. Import from an .xlsx or .csv using the template on the welcome screen, or export a Foreman workspace and bring the invoices across.</p><h3>Who is Ledger for?</h3><p>Australian sole traders and small trade businesses — electrical, plumbing, building, landscaping, painting and the like — who want to know their cash position and BAS exposure without paying for accounting software they don&#x27;t use.</p><p style="margin-top:18px;">Need a tool built around how your business works? <a href="../build/">Custom software, one tool, $2,000 fixed →</a></p></section>
