+<section class="seo-about" aria-labelledby="seo-about-h"><h2 id="seo-about-h">Takeoff — free plan takeoff and estimating for tradies</h2><p>Measure lengths, areas and counts off a PDF plan, price them with GST, export quote lines to Foreman. Free takeoff software for Australian trades.</p><h3>What plan formats can I measure from?</h3><p>PDF plans and common image formats (PNG, JPG). Drop the file in, pick a dimension you know — a 2,400 mm door opening, a 900 mm wall length — and Takeoff scales the whole sheet from it.</p><h3>How accurate is a takeoff from a PDF plan?</h3><p>As accurate as the plan and your calibration. Calibrate against the longest dimension you can find on the sheet; a plan at scale is typically within a percent or two, which is well inside the allowance most trades already carry for waste.</p><h3>Is Takeoff free?</h3><p>Yes, free forever. No trial period, no quote limits, no card. Nothing is uploaded — the plan and your measurements stay in your browser.</p><h3>Does it send the quote for me?</h3><p>Takeoff produces the priced scope. Export it as quote lines and it drops straight into Foreman, the free quoting and invoicing app in the same suite, which sends the quote and turns it into a job and a tax invoice.</p><h3>Can I use my own rates?</h3><p>Yes. Takeoff prices against your own price book — lineal, area and count rates — so a square metre of wall tiling or a downlight install is priced at what you actually charge.</p><h3>Which trades use plan takeoffs?</h3><p>Electrical, plumbing, tiling, painting, plastering, carpentry, flooring, landscaping, fencing and small building work — any job where the quantities are on a drawing before they&#x27;re on site.</p><p style="margin-top:18px;">Need a tool built around how your business works? <a href="../build/">Custom software, one tool, $2,000 fixed →</a></p></section>
